o</span></b></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">ved</span></b></span>. They like it better that way, given what the ways of The World are like; those who find independence too much to handle are still inclined to prefer the Devil they know over a different vast and incomprehensible king-and-country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:13:05-07:00","id":879237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879227#post879227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an android who regularly makes other androids who soon turn against him, Ultron proper is more classically in line with Prometheans, who <i>are</i> the adopted kids of the family, being coarse matter imbued with the chaotic spark of power and change that manifests in storms and sunshine and scintillating flame.<br /> <br /> Demons instead get to deal with the problems of being <span style=\"color:#000080\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">twice </span></b></span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">remo</span></b></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">ved</span></b></span>. They like it better that way, given what the ways of The World are like; those who find independence too much to handle are still inclined to prefer the Devil they know over a different vast and incomprehensible king-and-country.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, still doesn't make them less two faced me thinks. If you can call a walking steam engine family, you can call a hyper advanced techno-spiritual robot a twice removed cousin lol.<br /> <br /> Then again, that demons are the odd men out has always made me salty, its just so hypocritical when you look at how Beast was originally supposed to be and how they said that Beasts considered the other residents of the world/chronicles of darkness Kin. I highly dislike one of my favorite splats being relegated to being Zoidberg is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-01-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:42:54-07:00","id":879262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879237#post879237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, still doesn't make them less two faced me thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>If there is any splat that doesn't get to throw stones about being two-faced it is demons.</i></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can call a walking steam engine family, you can call a hyper advanced techno-spiritual robot a twice removed cousin lol. </div> </div> </div>The walking steam engine has a force where its heart would be that resonates with the terrifying house of horrors that the Begotten emerge from. The techno-religious robot has no connections to anything that it does not manually acquire or retain from its time under its similarly-denatured former employer.<br /> <br /> The family angle of Beast is relational/taxonomical before anything else and Demon is built on the fact that relations are unreliable for beings whose continued existence is purely declarative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, that demons are the odd men out has always made me salty, </div> </div> </div>I doubt that, seeing as salt dissipates upon fulfilling its grand purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> its just so hypocritical </div> </div> </div>Not what that word means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> when you look at how Beast was originally supposed to be and how they said that Beasts considered the other residents of the world/chronicles of darkness Kin. I highly dislike one of my favorite splats being relegated to being Zoidberg is all. </div> </div> </div>Being the weird squid-alien to the collection of feral children and earthborn automatons and freaky sewer mutants of the rest of the setting is kind of part of the point of being a demon drawn from the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:30:13-07:00","id":879293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879262#post879262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>If there is any splat that doesn't get to throw stones about being two-faced it is demons.</i></b><br /> <br /> The walking steam engine has a force where its heart would be that resonates with the terrifying house of horrors that the Begotten emerge from. The techno-religious robot has no connections to anything that it does not manually acquire or retain from its time under its similarly-denatured former employer.<br /> <br /> The family angle of Beast is relational/taxonomical before anything else and Demon is built on the fact that relations are unreliable for beings whose continued existence is purely declarative.<br /> <br /> I doubt that, seeing as salt dissipates upon fulfilling its grand purpose.<br /> <br /> Not what that word means.<br /> <br /> Being the weird squid-alien to the collection of feral children and earthborn automatons and freaky sewer mutants of the rest of the setting is kind of part of the point of being a demon drawn from the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Of course, they can be anywhere from two, to three, to an even greater number of faces.<br /> <br /> 2. Not entirely, if anything the Principle has more in common with the God-Machine in a diametrically opposed fashion than the primordial chaos and supernatural fear the Dark Mother represents from what I understand of the supernatural nature of the game's universe.<br /> <br /> 3. You seem to misunderstand the nuance and implications of what Cover signifies if that's all you've taken from it.<br /> <br /> 5. I guess, though in being Unchained one is no longer fully an outsider, they are as part of the world as the earthbound automaton or the sewer dwelling mutant or the feral child. Their genesis does not change this fact, it only offers a novel introduction and reinterpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:43:56-07:00","id":879297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879293#post879293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Not entirely, if anything the Principle has more in common with the God-Machine in a diametrically opposed fashion than the primordial chaos and supernatural fear the Dark Mother represents from what I understand of the supernatural nature of the game's universe.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intelligence Operations: The Principle and Qashmallim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The similarities these entities share with the Machine and its angels are immediate and striking, but they end as immediately as they begin.</b> The God-Machine is a constructed being, made of factories, engines, and power plants; it affects the world according to staggeringly elaborate conspiratorial schemes, and it uses Essence as its universal fuel. The Principle, on the other hand, is almost a gestalt consciousness that comes and goes as Pyros gathers or disseminates. It is an agent of change in any and all forms, using the enigmatic qashmallim to bring forth creation or destruction to suit its own passing whims.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. You seem to misunderstand the nuance and implications of what Cover signifies if that's all you've taken from it. </div> </div> </div>A set that starts with its sole member derived from Set B does, in fact, have no discernible connection to Set A in the big old relationship web of Where Things Come From.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. I guess, though in being Unchained one is no longer fully an outsider, they are as part of the world as the earthbound automaton or the sewer dwelling mutant or the feral child. Their genesis does not change this fact, it only offers a novel introduction and reinterpretation. </div> </div> </div>Genesis is the entire basis of Kinship. It's why the Begotten tend to frame the Dark Mother as the First Monster - because the things that make monsters have things in common with the protean nightmare that haunts humanity's collective soul in the same way that the Dreamborn serve as the psychic template for snakes and lakes and stones.<br /> <br /> If the core essence of Lahabiel the Shield still exists in any form it was cooked up decades to eons ago by something that doesn't have any relation to humanity it didn't put there itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:57:21-07:00","id":879305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879297#post879297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A set that starts with its sole member derived from Set B does, in fact, have no discernible connection to Set A in the big old relationship web of Where Things Come From.<br /> <br /> Genesis is the entire basis of Kinship. It's why the Begotten tend to frame the Dark Mother as the First Monster - because the things that make monsters have things in common with the protean nightmare that haunts humanity's collective soul in the same way that the Dreamborn serve as the psychic template for snakes and lakes and stones.<br /> <br /> If the core essence of Lahabiel the Shield still exists in any form it was cooked up decades to eons ago by something that doesn't have any relation to humanity it didn't put there itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The similarities do not end so quickly, in fact the similarities continue on and on metaphysically when one looks at the Principle in greater depth- depth that is not explored in demon. So unfortunately citing that section of the stg does little, if anything to sway me otherwise.<br /> <br /> I know how Kinship works.. I just don't agree with it due to how it works.<br /> <br /> And the God-Machine does have some intrinsic, if nebulous connection to humanity, so that logic is not as sound as it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T23:18:19-07:00","id":879319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879305#post879305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The similarities do not end so quickly, in fact the similarities continue on and on metaphysically when one looks at the Principle in greater depth</div> </div> </div> </div>I have read the entirety of Promethean 1e and the whole of the devblogs for 2e. There <i>is</i> no &quot;greater depth&quot; to explore in those that is not raw here's-some-options theory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know how Kinship works.. I just don't agree with it due to how it works. </div> </div> </div>Unconvinced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the God-Machine does have some intrinsic, if nebulous connection to humanity, so that logic is not as sound as it could be. </div> </div> </div>I do not have an intrinsic connection to my car, nebulous or otherwise, and I wouldn't do even if I built it myself from parts I made from materials I extracted myself from land I found myself.<br /> <br /> I do not have this connection to my car and the God-Machine operates at a further metaphorical remove than that. No amount of imparted data and stored virulent plagues will make it the Heavenly Father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T23:40:18-07:00","id":879328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879319#post879319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read the entirety of Promethean 1e and the whole of the devblogs for 2e. There <i>is</i> no &quot;greater depth&quot; to explore in those that is not raw here's-some-options theory.<br /> <br /> Unconvinced.<br /> <br /> I do not have an intrinsic connection to my car, nebulous or otherwise, and I wouldn't do even if I built it myself from parts I made from materials I extracted myself from land I found myself.<br /> <br /> I do not have this connection to my car and the God-Machine operates at a further metaphorical remove than that. No amount of imparted data and stored virulent plagues will make it the Heavenly Father.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you need to read again my friend, because there is more than just potential story hook options.<br /> <br /> That's nice, I don't really care if you are convinced- you've yet to convince me of anything either, your knowledge of promethean being suspect at this moment in fact.<br /> <br /> You as an individual does not equate to humanity's creativity and that creativity's expression through technology- which is what allowed mankind to survive and thrive and dominate the world it calls home. The God-Machine may be an alien techgnostic entity, but all technology is connected to the Machine to some extent, and the Machine in turn deeply reliant in humanity to ensure the vast majority of its occult matrices achieve output- that is as intrinsic a connection as I can see.<br /> <br /> Actually I will retract what I previously stated about you the individual not equating. The fact that you are utilising the tools and the materials to build said car is a contributing motion for this intrinsic interconnection of mankind and technology, my apologies.<br /> <br /> But this has detracted enough from a humorous satirical thread that I intended it to be, which is saddening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-01-2016, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T09:29:27-07:00","id":879556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879328#post879328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine may be an alien techgnostic entity, but all technology is connected to the Machine to some extent, and the Machine in turn deeply reliant in humanity to ensure the vast majority of its occult matrices achieve output- that is as intrinsic a connection as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only out of pragmatism. We're already it's trained monkeys, to train other monkeys would be inefficient.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T10:52:36-07:00","id":879591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879556#post879556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only out of pragmatism. We're already it's trained monkeys, to train other monkeys would be inefficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pragmatism or benefice, it doesn't matter what the underlying motive is; both Machine and man are bound together in a tyrannical, but still symbiotic circle. ( some would say parasitic, but its more beneficial than that... As terrible as the status quo is. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T14:43:47-07:00","id":879701,"title":"","content":"Huh. I like this Mr. Exposition, certainly. As good of a name as Exampiel/Mr. Example is. Maybe they work together in the ICPAA? Either way, this was an enjoyable little snippet and I'd certainly love to see more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T15:32:31-07:00","id":879734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879591#post879591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pragmatism or benefice, it doesn't matter what the underlying motive is; both Machine and man are bound together in a tyrannical, but still symbiotic circle. ( some would say parasitic, but its more beneficial than that... As terrible as the status quo is. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the setting as written contradicts your assumption, so...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:58:18-07:00","id":879807,"title":"","content":"Reliant on humanity.<br /> <br /> *giggle*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T22:50:35-07:00","id":879925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879734#post879734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the setting as written contradicts your assumption, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>And other pieces of the support the assumption, so...<br /> <br /> And stating that the setting contradicts something means nothing really, every line has pieces that support or contradicts each other. In this case the existence of Infrastructure as a whole supports the symbiosis more than contradicts it - and even then you are free to state whatever you want in your headcanon, they are your stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-02-2016, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T22:51:39-07:00","id":879926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879807#post879807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reliant on humanity.<br /> <br /> *giggle*</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, unless you know of another world with seven billion pawns to build pieces of your body.<br /> <br /> Angels are sort of in limited numbers by comparison, and most Infrastructure sort of needs<br /> Work crews, doctors, guards; sacrifices. .. 90% of these being human. So yeah, reliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-02-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T23:07:54-07:00","id":879930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879701#post879701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I like this Mr. Exposition, certainly. As good of a name as Exampiel/Mr. Example is. Maybe they work together in the ICPAA? Either way, this was an enjoyable little snippet and I'd certainly love to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it too, I enjoy pseudo in character satire. Glad you enjoyed it!<br /> <br /> And I agree, I think Mr. Exposition makes for a good counterpart for Exampiel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T04:41:50-07:00","id":880049,"title":"","content":"While angels and demons have existed in humanity's collective consciousness since times immemorial, the creatures of the God-Machine only appropriate their names without being possessed of any deeper semblance to beings these terms usually denote. Stories of angels and demons stem from encounters with spirits of appropriate nature, certain Fae and Changelings, glimpses of the Supernal Realms trickling down through the Astral, the Quashmalim, sometimes other denizens of World of Darkness (certain vampires can appear as angelic or demonic - or both - and I'm sure a couple Beasts throughout the ages have contributed to the imagery as well) but the Unchained and the angels of the God-Machine are about the last thing one would imagine when thinking of demons and angels. The workings of the God-Machine are hidden not just from humanity's sight, but also from our racial memory, legends and folklore, and they don't inform our fears, hopes and dreams the way other supernatural creatures in the World of Darkness do.<br /> <br /> This is why demons find no common ancestry with Beasts - they have no place in the Primordial Dream because their existence is both alien to and removed from the human existence in a way other monsters' isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T06:12:30-07:00","id":880102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880049#post880049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While angels and demons have existed in humanity's collective consciousness since times immemorial, the creatures of the God-Machine only appropriate their names without being possessed of any deeper semblance to beings these terms usually denote. Stories of angels and demons stem from encounters with spirits of appropriate nature, certain Fae and Changelings, glimpses of the Supernal Realms trickling down through the Astral, the Quashmalim, sometimes other denizens of World of Darkness (certain vampires can appear as angelic or demonic - or both - and I'm sure a couple Beasts throughout the ages have contributed to the imagery as well) but the Unchained and the angels of the God-Machine are about the last thing one would imagine when thinking of demons and angels. The workings of the God-Machine are hidden not just from humanity's sight, but also from our racial memory, legends and folklore, and they don't inform our fears, hopes and dreams the way other supernatural creatures in the World of Darkness do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's only one interpretation (and/or Headcannon). Another equally valid one is that the God-Machine (and Its Angels and Demons) <i>are</i> the source of the age old Angels and Demons memes, and hence why they so quickly map to them. You can find examples of the old &quot;spiritual&quot; phenomenon throughout Descent's material, especially when you consider the perspectives of any natives in light of Clarke's Third law.<br /> <br /> And are you really saying the concept of an impersonal, nigh-omnipotent, nigh-omniscient super-intelligence that cares about you only as much as you are useful to it has nothing to do with mankind's fears?<br /> <hr /><br /> Can we get back on topic, though?<br /> <br /> What's the feasibility of Going Loud to make a really sweet Gadget you can't otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T07:07:28-07:00","id":880137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=879926#post879926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely, unless you know of another world with seven billion pawns to build pieces of your body.<br /> <br /> Angels are sort of in limited numbers by comparison, and most Infrastructure sort of needs<br /> Work crews, doctors, guards; sacrifices. .. 90% of these being human. So yeah, reliant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Investment is not the same as reliance. This horse called humanity can fail spectacularly and the God-Machine, if it's purpose does not revolve around humanity in some form or fashion, can still pick a whole new option to follow.<br /> <br /> Investment is not reliance. Humanity is useful, not valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T07:42:48-07:00","id":880158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880137#post880137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Investment is not reliance. Humanity is useful, not valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>First part is true. Second not so much - Usefulness <i>is</i> value. Just because something is not critical, doesn't mean it isn't valuable. And considering the efforts the Machine goes to, to maintain the status quo regarding humanity, it certainly seems that the G-M has some fairly broad tolerances regarding people (in aggregate, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T08:08:24-07:00","id":880171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880102#post880102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that's only one interpretation (and/or Headcannon). Another equally valid one is that the God-Machine (and Its Angels and Demons) <i>are</i> the source of the age old Angels and Demons memes, and hence why they so quickly map to them. You can find examples of the old &quot;spiritual&quot; phenomenon throughout Descent's material, especially when you consider the perspectives of any natives in light of Clarke's Third law.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's any cultural background on this Earth that would warrant identifying a biomechanical grotesque with razorblade wings and riveter arm as either angel or demon. Even in our age, it's just too far beyond the expectations these words bring. Coupled with the fact that the same world is also inhabited by messenger-beings floating on wings of literal divine fire, spirits that can look exactly as angels and demons of legends, and horned Fae who trick people into horrible deals and/or abduct them into hellish landscapes, the creatures of the god-machine strike me as the <i>least</i> likely source of the mythic archetypes discussed.<br /> <br /> Not that your interpretation is impossible, but I do find it extremely unlikely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And are you really saying the concept of an impersonal, nigh-omnipotent, nigh-omniscient super-intelligence that cares about you only as much as you are useful to it has nothing to do with mankind's fears? </div> </div> </div>I am saying that it's an exceedingly modern concept. Since time immemorial, people have been imagining gods of varying shapes, powers and attitudes towards humanity. Some were anthropomorphic, some animalistic or monstrous, others had no shape that human senses could perceive. Some were patrons of particular places or actions, others held broad and powerful but clearly defined dominions, others yet were actually omnipotent. Some helped us, some tormented us, some of them made demands of us, their intent ranging from petty to malevolent to benevolent. But only in the last couple centuries did we consider the possibility of a divine being utterly indifferent to us, or using us in a strictly utilitarian fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T08:09:32-07:00","id":880172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880137#post880137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Investment is not the same as reliance. This horse called humanity can fail spectacularly and the God-Machine, if it's purpose does not revolve around humanity in some form or fashion, can still pick a whole new option to follow.<br /> <br /> Investment is not reliance. Humanity is useful, not valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it didnt rely on humanity, it would hardly, if ever make use of humanity as tools. But since it recognizes human kind's worth as a whole and uses humans for nearly every Project... its pretty reliant on mankind.<br /> <br /> and if you have an investment in something, you are reliant upon it bearing results, because you know ( or think you know) that it will achieve the results you require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T08:17:51-07:00","id":880176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880102#post880102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What's the feasibility of Going Loud to make a really sweet Gadget you can't otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, don't do it. Hours of being in demonic form to build a Gadget after going loud is pretty suicidal unless you are utterly safe-which is impossible with that sort of Aetheric Resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T08:54:26-07:00","id":880196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880172#post880172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it didnt rely on humanity, it would hardly, if ever make use of humanity as tools. But since it recognizes human kind's worth as a whole and uses humans for nearly every Project... its pretty reliant on mankind.<br /> <br /> and if you have an investment in something, you are reliant upon it bearing results, because you know ( or think you know) that it will achieve the results you require.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're enforcing my point here. Tools are that: tools. You don't grow attached to your tools (unless you have some psychic imbalance). The Machine uses humans because they're easier to manipulate than say, lemurs.<br /> <br /> If it had to use lemurs, it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:11:01-07:00","id":880205,"title":"","content":"I am invested in my car, but I suddenly lose it, it's not like I can't walk to all the pertinent places I need to in my life. I am not reliant on my car.*<br /> <br /> Barring the possibility that humanity is the whole of it's point, the God-Machine could nuke the species and not give a metaphorical shit the next day when it's making it's metaphorical coffee. It will just slowly drink in the savory implications of it's metaphorical coffee, figuratively let out a long sigh, and then &quot;get up&quot; and get back to work.<br /> <br /> *Or at least, this would be true if I had a car. I don't. I borrow a car from time to time. Which just makes the point even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:11:43-07:00","id":880206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880196#post880196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're enforcing my point here. Tools are that: tools. You don't grow attached to your tools (unless you have some psychic imbalance). The Machine uses humans because they're easier to manipulate than say, lemurs.<br /> <br /> If it had to use lemurs, it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary: humans grow attached to their tools, preferring to use their own to the exclusion of any others, putting little labels and decals on them, organizing them just so, becoming upset if someone else messes with them. After all, they're <i>your</i> tools; there's a sense of ownership, and that's an attachment. Same with cars; I can get by without my car, but when it was hit by another car and I couldn't drive it for a while, I missed it and wanted it back, even though I had a perfectly functional rental.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the G-M isn't human, but that doesn't preclude it growing attached.<br /> <br /> On-topic question: is it okay to go loud in response to being cut off in traffic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:15:28-07:00","id":880209,"title":"","content":"I wonder if going loud to win an argument would be a good idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:42:03-07:00","id":880226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880209#post880209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if going loud to win an argument would be a good idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you need access to Devil's Advocate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:45:00-07:00","id":880228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880206#post880206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the contrary: humans grow attached to their tools, preferring to use their own to the exclusion of any others, putting little labels and decals on them, organizing them just so, becoming upset if someone else messes with them. After all, they're <i>your</i> tools; there's a sense of ownership, and that's an attachment. Same with cars; I can get by without my car, but when it was hit by another car and I couldn't drive it for a while, I missed it and wanted it back, even though I had a perfectly functional rental.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the G-M isn't human, but that doesn't preclude it growing attached.<br /> <br /> On-topic question: is it okay to go loud in response to being cut off in traffic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mourn the loss of your tools like you would the loss of a pet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:48:03-07:00","id":880231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880228#post880228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mourn the loss of your tools like you would the loss of a pet?</div> </div> </div> </div> i know people who would cry at the loss of their car.<br /> <br /> some people see pet (and even other people) as nothing more than tools while other see some tools as having priceless intimate values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:56:36-07:00","id":880243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880171#post880171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's any cultural background on this Earth that would warrant identifying a biomechanical grotesque with razorblade wings and riveter arm as either angel or demon. Even in our age, it's just too far beyond the expectations these words bring. Coupled with the fact that the same world is also inhabited by messenger-beings floating on wings of literal divine fire, spirits that can look exactly as angels and demons of legends, and horned Fae who trick people into horrible deals and/or abduct them into hellish landscapes, the creatures of the god-machine strike me as the <i>least</i> likely source of the mythic archetypes discussed.<br /> <br /> Not that your interpretation is impossible, but I do find it extremely unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, to stone and early bronze-age tribesmen, &quot;Biomechanical&quot; is utterly indistinguishable from &quot;magical&quot;. Or the fact than not all Angels and Demon use the same &quot;Bio/Diesel-Punk&quot; aesthetic. It's not a rivet arm, its a maw that shoots spikes. These people wouldn't even know what &quot;rivet&quot; is, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880171#post880171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am saying that it's an exceedingly modern concept. Since time immemorial, people have been imagining gods of varying shapes, powers and attitudes towards humanity. Some were anthropomorphic, some animalistic or monstrous, others had no shape that human senses could perceive. Some were patrons of particular places or actions, others held broad and powerful but clearly defined dominions, others yet were actually omnipotent. Some helped us, some tormented us, some of them made demands of us, their intent ranging from petty to malevolent to benevolent. But only in the last couple centuries did we consider the possibility of a divine being utterly indifferent to us, or using us in a strictly utilitarian fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myths regarding Zeus (and other gods) drowning humanity because they were a nuisance don't agree with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:18:38-07:00","id":880261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880206#post880206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the contrary: humans grow attached to their tools, preferring to use their own to the exclusion of any others, putting little labels and decals on them, organizing them just so, becoming upset if someone else messes with them. After all, they're <i>your</i> tools; there's a sense of ownership, and that's an attachment. Same with cars; I can get by without my car, but when it was hit by another car and I couldn't drive it for a while, I missed it and wanted it back, even though I had a perfectly functional rental.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the G-M isn't human, but that doesn't preclude it growing attached.<br /> <br /> On-topic question: is it okay to go loud in response to being cut off in traffic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; there are lots of artists, workers and mechanics I personally know who are very adamant about their tools being an extension of themselves, myself included.<br /> <br /> If you are being a sacrificial lamb or making a Last Stand, sure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:20:09-07:00","id":880266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880228#post880228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mourn the loss of your tools like you would the loss of a pet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to the same degree, but sure, there's a feeling of loss. I've ever reached for my old pocketknife and found it not there, then remembered it was lost, and feel kinda sad about it before moving on. I've ever thought about the car I drove in high school, and wondered what became of it, with a feeling of nostalgia. Just because the feeling is not as strong as the loss of something else doesn't mean there's no attachment. &quot;Needing to go through a grieving process&quot; isn't a valid metric for determining if you are attached to something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880261#post880261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed; there are lots of artists, workers and mechanics I personally know who are very adamant about their tools being an extension of themselves, myself included.<br /> <br /> If you are being a sacrificial lamb or making a Last Stand, sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>A last stand against all those who refuse to use a blinker? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:37:46-07:00","id":880280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880228#post880228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mourn the loss of your tools like you would the loss of a pet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I had a laptop for years and years. That laptop had taken innumerable beatings and survived more close calls than I care to count. In all honesty it was a piece of shit and I had every opportunity to upgrade to something better, but it got the job done. My career, my classes, my life depended on that computer. And when it finally died, I wept like a little boy who lost his dog.<br /> <br /> I got a new computer a couple months later and it is a far better machine, but I still look back and get nostalgic when I remember all that old computer accomplished. <br /> <br /> The god-machine is an alien gestalt of Essence, Aether, and Incomprehensible technologies... but like any builder, it does not forget what is useful. Now does that mean the Machine would hesitate in replacing us? No. <br /> <br /> But that which comes after I can almost guarantee will be based off us, if more obedient and pliant. Mechopolis is a prime example that humans are still the most preferable servants besides angels. It could have anything from robot servitors , cryptids, and the like and what does it choose? Cyborg Stigmatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:48:31-07:00","id":880286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880266#post880266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A last stand against all those who refuse to use a blinker? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, people need to learn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:58:39-07:00","id":880291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880209#post880209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if going loud to win an argument would be a good idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you verbally bitch slap a Beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T11:23:52-07:00","id":880305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880206#post880206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, the G-M isn't human, but that doesn't preclude it growing attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kinda does, actually.<br /> <br /> Was the hitching of the &quot;mid-level schemer gets dragged by the drones into the reconfiguration chamber desperately screaming about how they can't do this to him&quot; trope to unlucky God-Machine patsies not an obvious tip-off that this efficiency-minded neither-cruel-nor-kind System only displays a humanlike semblance of attachment as a function of subterfuge or risk-management that promptly vanishes the instant it turns out to be less trouble to just scrap that branch of the Plan and find a workable alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T11:50:57-07:00","id":880318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880305#post880305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda does, actually.<br /> <br /> Was the hitching of the &quot;mid-level schemer gets dragged by the drones into the reconfiguration chamber desperately screaming about how they can't do this to him&quot; trope to unlucky God-Machine patsies not an obvious tip-off that this efficiency-minded neither-cruel-nor-kind System only displays a humanlike semblance of attachment as a function of subterfuge or risk-management that promptly vanishes the instant it turns out to be less trouble to just scrap that branch of the Plan and find a workable alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one story of the G-M, sure. It doesn't tell us what it was thinking, if it had regret about having to reconfigure that human, or if it felt that the reconfigurement wasn't destruction, but repair. Heck, the G-M having feelings is a great explanation as to why it's so faulty; maybe parts of it feel attachment to its minions and try show mercy, other parts are utterly efficient automata and destroy anything imperfect, other parts take glee in vengence or destruction or memes or whatever. The only facts that're consistent about the G-M is that it is unknowable and that it is imperfect. What the truth behind it is, and what form that imperfection takes, is an exercise for the ST/player/reader/chronicle. For some, it being the ultimate pragmatist is the best story; for others, being a moody and capricious deity is. <br /> <br /> I can't prove the G-M gets attached to humans. But I don't think you can prove that it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T11:58:25-07:00","id":880323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/878832-when-you-should-not-go-loud-an-instructional-video?p=880318#post880318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only facts that're consistent about the G-M is that it is unknowable and that it is imperfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire section of the corebook on playing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p241-242</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The God-Machine is neither cruel nor kind.</b> It uses whatever it calculates as necessary force in any situation, with a preference toward subtlety. Demons can avoid provoking it by staying off the radar, but once the God-Machine decides that the damage a ring will cause if left unchecked now outweighs the potential collateral damage when it strikes against them, it will send angels to hunt them down. On the other hand, if a stigmatic escapes from the God-Machine\u2019s control by persuading another human to take her place, the God-Machine won\u2019t pursue her \u2014 there\u2019s no point, as long as the gears keep turning.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> <b>The God-Machine doesn\u2019t think like a human,</b> doesn\u2019t show any emotions, and doesn\u2019t get frustrated. If it\u2019s prevented from gaining the desired output through one set of Infrastructure, it tries another.<br /> <br /> <b>The God-Machine thinks of people as roles</b> and only very rarely as individuals. As a being made of Infrastructure, it understands humans and supernatural creatures through the systems they place around themselves. Most humans <u>are</u> their jobs, their place in their families, and the resources they consume, as far as the God-Machine is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-02-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:51:18-07:00","id":880435,"title":"","content":"In other words, it very well may have emotions, its just impossible to discern by beings on such such a tiny scale as we are. While it is a machine like any other, the Storyteller is always free to give it quirks to an extent. Its not gonna become glaDOS, SHODAN, or AM, but there is definitely a personality to the Machine, albeit mechanical, ponderous and languid as it calculates the flow and ebb of the universe and how its plans fit into the skein of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-02-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"